    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n435" root="ادب" body-key="A">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدِرَ</span></b> , aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اَدَبَ</span></b> , (T, M, Msb, K,) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدَرٌ</span> (Lth,
T, S, Mgh) and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَدَرَةٌ</span>, (Lth, TA,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُدْرَةٌ</span>, (as in
the TT,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُدْرَةٌ</span> is a simple subst., (M, K,) and
so is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُدْرَةٌ</span>, (K,) <i>He</i> (a man, S) <i>had the disorder
termed</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أُدْرَةٌ</span>. (T, S, M, &amp;c.)

